# Vercel-style redirects scaffold for v1.4 Astro migration.
#
# NOTE: This file is currently INERT — vercel.json still points at the bash
# build, which serves `index.html` from the repo root. These rules will only
# take effect after `vercel.json` is flipped to `{ "framework": "astro",
# "outputDirectory": "dist" }` at merge time.
#
# Strategy for legacy hash URLs (e.g. https://.../#patterns):
#   The legacy SPA used `#<slug>` for routing. Hash fragments are NEVER sent
#   to the server, so server-side redirects can't catch them. Instead,
#   src/layouts/Doc.astro contains an inline pre-paint script that checks
#   `location.hash`, maps it to `/<slug>/`, and `history.replaceState`s.
#   That script will be added as part of the bulk-migration follow-up; the
#   stub below is for any future *path* redirects we discover during the
#   visual diff.

# Example (uncomment when needed):
# /old-slug   /new-slug   301
